# Audit report -- Phase 272: two bounded defects, and a gate change deferred

**Verdict**: PASS
**Target**: docs/plan-qor-phase272-three-bounded-gate-defects.md (iteration 3)
**Session**: 2026-09-08T0215-322b7e
**Issues**: GH #426, GH #433 (GH #424 deferred)
**Mode**: adversarial; one review round by design, reviewer holding Read/Grep/Glob only
**Iterations**: 3 (iteration 1 VETOed; D1 deferred, D3 inverted)

## Scope

Covers that advance writes the marker the staleness check reads, and that two misleading messages are corrected without altering the guard they describe. Neither changes what any gate decides, which is the scope line that earned one review round.

## Blocking grounds raised and cleared

1. D3 was inverted: the raise on a non-release change_class is the guard, not the defect, and four sealed plans in this repository prove the class works. Mapping it to a patch bump would have created two contradicting definitions across three callers.
2. The test drafted with it would have pinned the proposition an earlier phase rejected.
3. D1 was not bounded: an enumerated verdict vocabulary fails open, the proposed factoring would have inverted the gate so a VETO authorizes a seal, and the refusal would have diagnosed the wrong fault. Deferred with its constraint set preserved.
4. A CI command named a test file that does not exist; the affected-files list named a module with no coverage of the changed function; the scope note described three defects after the title said two.

## Limits

The reviewer executed nothing. Every measurement is the author's. It confirmed by reading that the one-marker change breaks no existing test, and that this repository carries exactly one matching marker, so the fix is latent here and live for the consumer that filed it.
